# Private Rooms & Fanout (Phase 5B.1 / 5B.2)

- Laravel alone authorizes room membership. Node never queries PostgreSQL for ACL.
- Room access requires a one-use REST grant (`WS_ROOM_GRANT_REDIS_PREFIX`), redeemed with atomic `GETDEL` inside an already-authenticated socket. Never accept client `player_id` / open `room_id` as authority.
- Bind grant `user_id` to the authenticated socket identity before `room.subscribed`.
- Fanout only to: (1) `target_user_id` personal sockets, or (2) sockets with an active authorized room subscription for `target_room_id`.
- Known hint types use strict payloads: `pvp.room.changed`, `pvp.invitation.changed`, `pvp.battle.changed` (`room_id`, `battle_id`, `version`, `last_event_sequence` only), `room.subscription.revoked`.
- Hint delivery is best-effort: Redis Pub/Sub for the persistent server, async Lambda invoke for the Lambda adapter (`src/lambda/`). Keep both on the same envelope and validation. Clients must rehydrate via REST. Fail closed for private fanout when Redis is unavailable.
- No combat calculations, XP, battle actions, or combat secrets in Node or on the wire.
- On `room.subscription.revoked` / room close, drop local subscriptions.
